\f1\b \cf0 Christmas \'97 Sarah confronts Eloise
\f0\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Redraft around trust rather than technology.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Sarah/Eloise relationship; pregnancy stress; waters breaking.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Sarah now has all three pieces: capability, precedent, concealment. Her accusation is essentially: 
\f1\b you knew what this might become, you knew because you had been here before, and you let me continue without telling me.
\f0\b0  Eloise defends continued research as necessary and scientifically justified. Both should have arguments. The rupture becomes personal enough to trigger the birth sequence.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Avoid reducing the fight to \'93weapons bad / science good\'94.\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The main drafting dependencies are important. 
\f1\b Do 30 Sep and 1 Oct first
\f0\b0 , because they determine exactly what Hayley already knows. Then redraft 
\f1\b 25\'9626 Nov as a pair
\f0\b0 ; the first scene should deliver the historical evidence, the second should interpret it and give Sarah agency. Only after those are stable should you revise the December experiment sequence, because the December scenes need to pay off language and concepts planted in November.\
For 
\f1\b 25 November
\f0\b0 , I would preserve your current first two paragraphs almost untouched:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After the census, Hayley turned her attention back on whether Eloise had any weapons projects shadowing Project Kebab.\
and the zombie-corpse paragraph.\
Then the current Chip paragraph should be replaced by a transition based on 
\f1\b Hayley already knowing the public Rotherhithe story and deciding to follow what came after it
\f0\b0 . That is the key structural correction.\
The investigation scene should probably produce four concrete documents or facts, no more: the Rotherhithe-derived research trail; the Shakti project\'92s legitimate declared purpose; the Fridge Force finding that deliberate manipulation had produced controllable displaced effects; Eloise\'92s appeal. That is sufficient. Do not let Hayley conveniently solve the entire history of the project.\
For 
\f1\b 26 November
\f0\b0 , the exposition should be divided so Hayley explains 
\f1\b what happened historically
\f0\b0 , while Sarah asks the questions that reveal 
\f1\b why it matters to Kebab
\f0\b0 . The holoscreen belongs here because it solves a practical problem: Hayley has material she does not want on Shakti infrastructure. Sarah\'92s \'93this was my mother\'92s\'94 can be almost incidental. The scene then makes Sarah indispensable rather than pregnant furniture.\
The dream-pattern connection should develop in three steps across the arc. In November Sarah sees only a 
\f1\b family resemblance
\f0\b0  between her patterns and the historical interference maps. During the December experiments the patterns become more ordered as the discs become more coherent. After Missing Socks/Gibson she realises some of the incoming information may describe or determine 
\f1\b relationships between the discs themselves
\f0\b0 . Only then does the possibility of targeting emerge.\
The technical escalation should also stay very simple:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Rotherhithe:
\f0\b0  interacting fields can create displaced effects.\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b Old Shakti project:
\f0\b0  displacement can be influenced.\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b Kebab:
\f0\b0  coherent five-disc operation produces a remote effect at a mathematically determined locus.\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b Final evidence:
\f0\b0  Eloise knew enough about this lineage to recognise what Kebab was becoming.\
That is all the technical apparatus you need. Extra pseudo-physics will make the arc harder to follow rather than more convincing.\
For 
\f1\b Missing Socks
\f0\b0 , I would preserve the absurd message and probably some of the narrator\'92s extended sock cosmology, though the current version is much too long for the dramatic position. The important tonal trick is that the joke should momentarily 
\f1\b release the pressure
\f0\b0 . Everyone has been worrying about Rotherhithe and dangerous coherence; then the first voice from another universe asks about missing socks. The reader gets permission to laugh. The post-run discovery of Gibson then turns the exact same success sinister.\
For 
\f1\b Weaponizing the Unknown
\f0\b0 , I would reconstruct rather than line-edit the rough. Its current dialogue repeatedly makes the same point and gives away intent far too early. The new scene should revolve around one discovery: 
\f1\b Gibson was not random
\f0\b0 . It sits where the field geometry says a reinforcement locus should have been. The argument then becomes whether this is coincidence, side effect, or capability. Eloise can reasonably demand further evidence; Chip can reasonably insist that Fridge Force has seen enough of this pattern before; Sarah now understands why Hayley\'92s November material mattered.\
Finally, I would leave a deliberate 
\f1\b evidentiary hole
\f0\b0  between Weaponizing and Christmas. After Weaponizing, Sarah should know that Kebab 
\f3\i can probably do something terrifying
\f0\i0 . She should still lack a reason to believe Eloise deliberately hid that trajectory from her. The bridge scene supplies that missing personal fact. Without that gap, the Christmas confrontation will always feel delayed.\
The working test for every revision is therefore:\

\f1\b After this scene, does Sarah know enough to be more worried, but still have a credible reason not to confront Eloise yet?
\f0\b0 \
Until Christmas, the answer should always be 
\f1\b yes
\f0\b0 .\
}